   → All problems!              ↓
                           Spark reads it
                           → All problems SOLVED!
How Delta Lake Solves Every Problem
✅ Solution 1 — Transaction Log (_delta_log)
This is the heart of Delta Lake!
Your Delta Table Folder in S3:
├── _delta_log/
│     ├── 000000.json  → "Added file1.parquet with 1 lakh records"
│     ├── 000001.json  → "Added file2.parquet with 50k records"
│     ├── 000002.json  → "Deleted 20k records matching id > 5000"
│     └── 000003.json  → "Schema changed - added new column"
├── file1.parquet
├── file2.parquet
└── file3.parquet
Every single change is recorded in JSON log files
This is what enables ACID, Time Travel, Audit everything!
✅ Solution 2 — ACID Transactions
Pipeline A writing data  ──┐
                            ├→ Delta Lake manages using Transaction Log
Pipeline B writing data  ──┘

→ Each write is ATOMIC — either fully completes or fully rolls back
→ No more partial/corrupted data!
✅ Solution 3 — Update, Delete, Merge Now Possible!
-- GDPR Delete request
DELETE FROM customers WHERE customer_id = 12345;

-- Update salary
UPDATE employees SET salary = 60000 WHERE emp_id = 101;

-- Upsert (Insert if not exists, Update if exists)
MERGE INTO target t
USING source s ON t.id/ = s.id/
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET t.salary = s.salary
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;
All of this impossible in plain Data Lake — possible in Delta Lake!
✅ Solution 4 — Time Travel
-- What was the data yesterday?
SELECT * FROM employees VERSION AS OF 5;

-- What was the data on specific date?
SELECT * FROM employees 
TIMESTAMP AS OF '2024-01-15 10:00:00';

-- Oops accidentally deleted data? RESTORE it!
RESTORE TABLE employees TO VERSION AS OF 10;
✅ Solution 5 — Schema Enforcement
Delta Table schema: name STRING, salary INT

Someone tries to write: { "name": 123, "salary": "fifty thousand" }
                                    ↓
                        Delta Lake REJECTS it! ❌
                        "Schema mismatch — write blocked"
                        
→ Bad data never enters your table!
✅ Solution 6 — Auto Optimisation (Small File Problem Solved)
-- Delta Lake automatically compacts small files
OPTIMIZE employees;

-- Z-Order for faster queries
OPTIMIZE employees ZORDER BY (department, city);

-- Auto Optimize in Databricks — happens automatically!
