VACUUM, OPTIMIZE & AUTO OPTIMIZE — Complete Guide 🎯
PART 1 — VACUUM 🧹
What is VACUUM?
"VACUUM is a cleanup command that permanently deletes old parquet files from cloud storage that are no longer needed by Delta Lake"
Simple Analogy 🗑️
Think of your Phone Gallery
You delete a photo → it goes to Trash folder
Photo is deleted logically but still occupies storage!
VACUUM = Emptying the Trash permanently!
Why VACUUM is Needed?
When you UPDATE/DELETE in Delta Lake:

Old parquet file → Marked as "removed" in transaction log
                 → Still physically EXISTS in S3!
                 → Still costing you money!
                 → Kept for TIME TRAVEL purpose

Without VACUUM:
Day 1:  100GB
Day 30: 150GB  (50GB of old removed files accumulating)
Day 90: 200GB  (100GB waste — paying for useless files!)

With VACUUM:
Day 1:  100GB
Day 30: 100GB  ✅ (old files cleaned up!)
Day 90: 100GB  ✅ (storage stays clean!)
What Exactly VACUUM Deletes?
VACUUM deletes:
✅ Old parquet files marked as "removed" in transaction log
✅ Files that are no longer part of any active table version
✅ Orphan files (files that exist in S3 but not in transaction log)

VACUUM does NOT delete:
❌ Active parquet files (current data — NEVER touched!)
❌ Transaction log files (_delta_log)
❌ Files within retention period (recent files kept for time travel)
VACUUM Syntax
-- Basic VACUUM (default 7 days retention)
VACUUM employees;

-- Custom retention period
VACUUM employees RETAIN 168 HOURS;  -- 7 days
VACUUM employees RETAIN 24 HOURS;   -- 1 day
VACUUM employees RETAIN 0 HOURS;    -- Delete everything old immediately

-- DRY RUN — see what WILL be deleted without actually deleting
VACUUM employees DRY RUN;

-- Output of DRY RUN:
-- "Would delete: part-0001.parquet"
-- "Would delete: part-0045.parquet"
-- "Would delete: part-0123.parquet"
-- Useful to check before actually running!
Default Retention — Why 7 Days?
Delta Lake default retention = 7 days (168 hours)

Reason:
→ Keeps last 7 days of history for time travel
→ Gives engineers time to detect data issues
→ If pipeline writes wrong data on Monday
  → You have until Sunday to time travel and fix it!
→ After 7 days → old files deleted permanently

⚠️ CRITICAL WARNING:
VACUUM employees RETAIN 0 HOURS;

→ Deletes ALL old files immediately!
→ Time travel becomes IMPOSSIBLE!
→ Cannot recover any historical data!
→ Only do this if you are 100% sure!
When to Use VACUUM?
Use VACUUM when:
✅ Storage costs increasing unexpectedly
✅ S3/ADLS bill is too high
✅ Table has heavy UPDATE/DELETE operations daily
✅ After large data migrations or bulk deletes
✅ After GDPR delete requests
   (to permanently remove data from storage too!)

How frequently?
→ Tables with heavy changes → Run weekly
→ Tables with light changes → Run monthly
→ Automate using Databricks Jobs scheduler!
VACUUM Real World Example
Scenario: E-commerce orders table
→ 10 lakh orders updated daily (status changes)
→ Each update creates new parquet files
→ Old files accumulate

Without VACUUM (after 30 days):
Active data:     100GB
Old removed files: 85GB (waste!)
Total S3 cost:   185GB 😱

After VACUUM RETAIN 168 HOURS:
Active data:     100GB
Old files within 7 days: 15GB (kept for time travel)
Deleted:         70GB ✅
Total S3 cost:   115GB 💰 saved!

