🎯 Perfect Interview Answer
"Delta Lake has three key maintenance features.
VACUUM permanently deletes old parquet files that are marked as removed in the transaction log. When you update or delete rows, Delta keeps old files for time travel. VACUUM cleans them up after the retention period — default 7 days — to reclaim cloud storage costs. Without VACUUM, storage keeps growing even though data size hasnt changed.
OPTIMIZE solves the small files problem. Streaming pipelines and frequent writes create thousands of tiny parquet files. Too many small files slow down queries because Spark has to open each file separately. OPTIMIZE compacts them into fewer large files. Combined with ZORDER, it also physically co-locates related data together — enabling Delta Lake to skip irrelevant files completely during queries, making them dramatically faster.
Auto Optimize is Databricks-specific automation with two parts — Optimized Write which produces right-sized files during the write itself, and Auto Compact which automatically compacts small files in background after each write. This is ideal for streaming tables where manual OPTIMIZE scheduling is impractical.
Together — Auto Optimize prevents small files from forming, OPTIMIZE fixes them when they do, and VACUUM keeps storage costs under control!"
