Key Concepts in Structured Streaming
Trigger — How Often to Process?
# Process as fast as possible (default)
.trigger(processingTime='0 seconds')

# Process every 30 seconds
.trigger(processingTime='30 seconds')

# Process every 5 minutes
.trigger(processingTime='5 minutes')

# Process once and stop (like batch!)
.trigger(once=True)

# Process one batch and stop (newer way)
.trigger(availableNow=True)

Output Modes — How to Write?
# Append — only new rows written
# Good for: event data, logs
.outputMode("append")

# Complete — entire result rewritten
# Good for: aggregations, counts
.outputMode("complete")

# Update — only changed rows written
# Good for: running totals
.outputMode("update")
Checkpoint — Most Important! ⚠️
# Checkpoint saves streaming progress!
.option("checkpointLocation", "/checkpoints/mystream/")

Without checkpoint:
→ Cluster crashes
→ Stream restarts from BEGINNING!
→ Duplicate data! 😱

With checkpoint:
→ Cluster crashes
→ Stream restarts from where it STOPPED!
→ No duplicate data! ✅
→ Exactly once processing!
Watermark — Handle Late Data
# What if data arrives late?
# Example: Event happened at 10AM
#          But reached system at 10:30AM!

df.withWatermark("event_time", "30 minutes") \
  .groupBy(
      window("event_time", "10 minutes"),
      "region"
  ).sum("revenue")

# Means:
# Accept late data up to 30 minutes
# After 30 minutes → ignore late records
