Recommended ✅
🎯 Interview Answer
"Both trigger once and availableNow process all pending data and stop — making them behave like batch but with streaming benefits like checkpointing and incremental processing.
trigger once=True processes everything in a single massive batch and saves checkpoint only at the end — so if job fails you restart from beginning which is risky for large data.
trigger availableNow=True processes pending data in multiple smaller batches saving checkpoint after each batch — so failure recovery restarts from last successful batch not from beginning. It needs less memory, is more reliable and is the current Databricks recommended approach. trigger once is now deprecated in favor of availableNow!"

