Output modes in structured streaming?
output mode tells spart what to write to sink after each microbatch processing
APPEND  - write only new rows (only newly dded rows since last trigger are written to output - existing rows never touched)
COMPLETE - write entire result everytime(Entire result table is rewritten to output after every micro batch - every single row every time)
UPDATE - write only changed rows (only rows that were updated or newly added since last trigger are written - unchanged rows skipped)

For example if any row deleted in my source then?
APPEND AND UPDATE MODE - DELETES COMPLETELY IGNORED
Both above modes have no concept of deletion.
Only COMPLETE mode reflects deletions ( because it rewrites everything)

