cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode — Complete Guide 🎯
What is Schema Evolution in Streaming?
Day 1: Source JSON files have:
{ "order_id": 1, "amount": 100 }

Day 30: Source JSON files NOW have:
{ "order_id": 1, "amount": 100, "discount": 10 }
                                  ↑
                             NEW COLUMN ADDED!

Question: What should streaming job do?
→ Fail? Ignore? Accept? Rescue?

Answer depends on schemaEvolutionMode!
Setup — Where to Put It
df = spark.readStream \
    .format("cloudFiles") \
    .option("cloudFiles.format", "json") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaLocation",
            "abfss://container@storage/schema/orders/") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode",
            "addNewColumns") \         ← SET HERE!
    .load("abfss://container@storage/raw/orders/")
schemaLocation — Why Needed?
Before understanding modes
understand schemaLocation first!

schemaLocation:
→ Where Autoloader SAVES detected schema
→ Autoloader reads files → detects schema
→ Saves that schema to schemaLocation
→ Next run → reads saved schema first
→ Compares with new files schema

Without schemaLocation:
→ Autoloader detects schema fresh every run
→ Slow!
→ Schema inconsistency possible!

With schemaLocation:
→ Schema cached and reused ✅
→ Evolution tracked properly ✅
→ REQUIRED when using schemaEvolutionMode!
Four Schema Evolution Modes
Mode 1 — addNewColumns (Most Common ✅)
What it Does
New column arrives in source?
→ Automatically ADD that column
   to output table!
→ Old records get NULL for new column
→ Stream continues without interruption!
Example
Existing schema:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE

New file arrives with extra column:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE
discount  DOUBLE  ← NEW!

addNewColumns behavior:
→ Detects discount is new column
→ Automatically adds discount to table
→ Old records: discount = NULL
→ New records: discount = actual value
→ Stream keeps running! ✅
Code
df = spark.readStream \
    .format("cloudFiles") \
    .option("cloudFiles.format", "json") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaLocation",
            "abfss://container@storage/schema/") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode",
            "addNewColumns") \
    .load("abfss://container@storage/raw/")
When to Use
✅ Source adds new columns over time
✅ You want zero interruption streaming
✅ Bronze layer ingestion
✅ You don't know future schema changes
✅ Most production streaming pipelines
Mode 2 — none (Strict Mode)
What it Does
New column arrives?
→ IGNORE completely!
→ New column NOT added to output!
→ Stream continues but new column lost!

Existing column missing?
→ NULL values for that column

Data type changes?
→ Stream FAILS!
Example
Existing schema:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE

New file arrives:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE
discount  DOUBLE  ← NEW!

none behavior:
→ discount column IGNORED!
→ Not written to output table
→ Data silently dropped! ⚠️

Output always stays:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE
Code
df = spark.readStream \
    .format("cloudFiles") \
    .option("cloudFiles.format", "json") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaLocation",
            "abfss://container@storage/schema/") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode",
            "none") \
    .load("abfss://container@storage/raw/")
When to Use
✅ Schema is FIXED — never changes
✅ Downstream systems expect exact schema
✅ Silver/Gold layer processing
✅ When extra columns should be ignored
✅ Strict schema contract environments

⚠️ Warning:
New columns silently dropped!
No error — just data loss!
Easy to miss!
Mode 3 — failOnNewColumns (Safest ✅)
What it Does
New column arrives?
→ Stream FAILS immediately! ❌
→ Raises error loudly!
→ Forces team to review schema change
→ Manual intervention required
→ Resume only after explicit decision!
Example
Existing schema:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE

New file arrives:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE
discount  DOUBLE  ← NEW!

failOnNewColumns behavior:
→ Detects new column
→ FAILS with error:
  "New column 'discount' detected!
   Stream stopped!"
→ Team gets alert
→ Team reviews: should we add this column?
→ If yes → change mode to addNewColumns
→ If no → filter column at source
→ Restart stream
Code
df = spark.readStream \
    .format("cloudFiles") \
    .option("cloudFiles.format", "json") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaLocation",
            "abfss://container@storage/schema/") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode",
            "failOnNewColumns") \
    .load("abfss://container@storage/raw/")
When to Use
✅ Production critical pipelines
✅ Financial or regulated data
✅ Schema changes need approval process
✅ Team wants visibility of ALL changes
✅ When silent data loss is unacceptable
✅ Governance heavy environments
Mode 4 — rescue (Most Powerful ✅)
What it Does
New column arrives?
→ Does NOT add new column to table
→ Instead captures ALL unexpected data
   in special column called:
   _rescued_data
→ Nothing is lost!
→ Stream continues!
→ You can parse _rescued_data later!
Example
Existing schema:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE

New file arrives:
order_id  INT
amount    DOUBLE
discount  DOUBLE   ← NEW!
promo_code STRING  ← NEW!

rescue behavior:
Output table:
order_id | amount | _rescued_data
---------|--------|----------------------------------
1        | 100    | {"discount":10, "promo_code":"SAVE10"}
2        | 200    | {"discount":20, "promo_code":"FLAT20"}

→ New columns not added to main schema
→ But data NOT lost!
→ Captured in _rescued_data as JSON string
→ Parse later when needed!
Code
df = spark.readStream \
    .format("cloudFiles") \
    .option("cloudFiles.format", "json") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaLocation",
            "abfss://container@storage/schema/") \
    .option("cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode",
            "rescue") \
    .load("abfss://container@storage/raw/")
Parse Rescued Data Later
# Extract rescued data when needed
from pyspark.sql.functions import from_json, col

rescued_schema = "discount DOUBLE, promo_code STRING"

df_parsed = df.withColumn(
    "rescued_parsed",
    from_json(col("_rescued_data"), rescued_schema)
).select(
    "order_id",
    "amount",
    col("rescued_parsed.discount").alias("discount"),
    col("rescued_parsed.promo_code").alias("promo_code")
)
When to Use
✅ Cannot afford ANY data loss
✅ Schema changes unpredictable
✅ Want to investigate unexpected data
✅ Compliance — must capture everything
✅ Good for Bronze layer safety net
All Modes — Side by Side
Source sends new column "discount":

addNewColumns  → Add discount to table ✅
               → Old rows get NULL
               → Stream continues ✅

none           → Ignore discount ⚠️
               → Data silently dropped
               → Stream continues ✅

failOnNewColumns → FAIL loudly ❌
                → Team notified
                → Manual fix needed

rescue         → Keep discount in
               → _rescued_data column ✅
               → Nothing lost ✅
               → Stream continues ✅
