→ Simple one-off scripts
🎯 Interview Answer
"Delta Live Tables is Databricks declarative ETL framework where you declare what your pipeline should produce using simple Python decorators — Databricks automatically handles dependency resolution, failure retries, performance optimization and monitoring.
Key features are three dataset types — Streaming Tables for incremental processing, Materialized Views for aggregated results, and Views for intermediate logic. The most powerful feature is Expectations for built-in data quality — expect warns but keeps bad records, expect_or_drop removes bad records, expect_or_fail stops the entire pipeline.
DLT also supports CDC through APPLY CHANGES INTO which handles inserts, updates and deletes automatically. Pipelines run in Triggered mode for scheduled batch processing or Continuous mode for real time processing.
The biggest advantage over manual Spark ETL is the visual DAG showing entire pipeline lineage, built-in monitoring dashboard, automatic dependency ordering and zero boilerplate retry logic — making it the recommended approach for building production Medallion architecture pipelines in Databricks!"


