******important point
when you created workspace in azure databricks
databricks create two resource groups one is in your resource group and another one is
in azure search bar type "databricks-rg-yourworkspacename" then enter now you can see that internal managed resource group

**when you deploy azure databricks, azure splits the infrastructure into two distinct parts to keep the "software" separate 
from the "hardware".
1) The workspace resource group (your group)
this is the group you created and named. This of this as the front office
whats inside : just the azure databricks service (the UI/Portal)
who manages it : you can move it or delete it.
purpose : This is where you log in and create notebooks and manage users.

2) The managed resource group (The system group)
Azure creates this automatically (usually names databricks-rg-workspacename). This of this as a engine room.
whats inside: All the heavy machinery required to run your code.
 		- virtual machines : the actual servers (clusters) that process your data
		- storage account : the dbstorage account you found (used for systemlogs and dbfs)
		- Network (VNet): The private road where data travels
who manages it : Azure. It has a lock on it (Deny assignment) so you dont accidently delete a disk or a server that the databricks 
UI needs to function
Purpose : This is where the actual computation happens


